2. DEFINITIONS
======================================================================

2.1 "Vectra"

"Vectra" means the software, source code, object code, documentation,
configuration files, build files, scripts, tools, and other materials
distributed by the Copyright Holder under this License.

2.2 "Copyright Holder"

"Copyright Holder" means:

Driftless Software

2.3 "You"

"You" means an individual or legal entity exercising rights granted
under this License.

2.4 "Development"

"Development" means creating, modifying, compiling, debugging,
testing, benchmarking, porting, integrating, or otherwise engineering
Vectra or software based upon Vectra.

Development includes development performed by employees, contractors,
students, researchers, or other authorized personnel of an
organization.

2.5 "Evaluation"

"Evaluation" means examining or testing Vectra to determine whether
Vectra is suitable for a particular application, hardware platform,
product, service, or technical requirement.

2.6 "Prototype"

"Prototype" means a non-production implementation used for engineering,
testing, demonstration, experimentation, research, validation, or
proof-of-concept purposes.

A Prototype is not a Commercial Deployment merely because it operates
physical hardware or a physical robot.

2.7 "Commercial Deployment"

"Commercial Deployment" means deploying Vectra as part of a product,
system, device, robot, machine, appliance, embedded system, or other
commercial offering that is:

(a) sold;

(b) leased;

(c) rented;

(d) licensed;

(e) distributed;

(f) supplied to customers or end users;

(g) operated for customers or end users as a commercial service; or

(h) otherwise placed into production for the purpose of generating
    commercial revenue or commercial benefit.

(i) operated internally by an organization for production business
    operations, warehouse automation, manufacturing, or commercial 
    services, even if not directly sold or distributed to third parties.

Commercial Deployment begins when Vectra is incorporated into or used
by a production system intended for commercial operation or delivery
to customers or end users.

2.8 "Production"

"Production" means operational use of a system for its intended
commercial purpose rather than engineering, development, testing,
evaluation, research, demonstration, or prototyping.

