5. ACTIVITIES THAT DO NOT REQUIRE A COMMERCIAL LICENSE
======================================================================

The following activities do NOT constitute Commercial Deployment and
do NOT require payment under this License:

(a) downloading Vectra;

(b) reading or studying the source code;

(c) modifying Vectra;

(d) compiling Vectra;

(e) running Vectra on development hardware;

(f) running Vectra in QEMU or another emulator;

(g) running Vectra in a virtual machine;

(h) porting Vectra to a company's hardware;

(i) developing device drivers for Vectra;

(j) developing hardware support for Vectra;

(k) developing applications for Vectra;

(l) internal engineering;

(m) internal testing;

(n) internal benchmarking;

(o) security testing;

(p) debugging;

(q) academic research;

(r) educational use;

(s) hobbyist use;

(t) proof-of-concept systems;

(u) laboratory systems;

(v) development robots;

(w) prototype robots;

(x) demonstrations performed solely for engineering, research,
    evaluation, or sales-evaluation purposes; and

(y) determining whether Vectra is suitable for a future commercial
    product.

An organization may perform the activities above without purchasing
a commercial license, regardless of whether the organization is a
commercial entity.

For avoidance of doubt, an employee of a commercial company may
download, modify, compile, test, and evaluate Vectra as part of their
engineering work without requiring a commercial license, provided
that the activities do not constitute Commercial Deployment.

