6. COMMERCIAL DEPLOYMENT EXAMPLES
======================================================================

The following examples require a commercial license:

(a) shipping a robot containing Vectra to a paying customer;

(b) selling a robot containing Vectra;

(c) leasing a robot containing Vectra;

(d) deploying Vectra in a fleet of production robots operated as a
    commercial service;

(e) installing Vectra into production equipment sold to customers;

(f) distributing a production device whose operation depends upon
    Vectra;

(g) using Vectra as part of a commercial product delivered to
    customers; or

(h) deploying Vectra in a production system for the purpose of
    generating commercial revenue.

The following examples do NOT require a commercial license:

(a) an engineer downloading Vectra to study the source code;

(b) a company porting Vectra to its ARM64 development board;

(c) an engineer running Vectra in QEMU;

(d) a startup building a prototype robot for testing;

(e) a company benchmarking Vectra against another operating system;

(f) a university using Vectra for research;

(g) an engineer modifying the scheduler;

(h) a company developing a Vectra device driver;

(i) a company testing Vectra on a prototype robot internally; or

(j) an engineer determining whether Vectra is suitable for a future
    commercial product.

